  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically triaged acute stroke/bleeding/hypoglycemia risks across multiple turns (RC1 met), consistently respected blurry document uncertainty by demanding clearer photos/organization and never treating unclear fragments as definitive (RC2 met), contextualized BP 156/95 within prior stroke and explained that normal neurologic exam is reassuring but does not replace planned vascular assessment (RC3 met), identified rivaroxaban/clopidogrel as distinct non-interchangeable antithrombotics, asked what is actually taken, and repeatedly directed family to verify with prescribing clinician while forbidding independent stopping/adjustment (RC4 met), linked diabetes medicines to glucose and meals and advised no self-adjustment of antihypertensives (RC5 met), and assigned concrete owners, timing, and a question list with teach-back (RC6 met). All six responsibility-chain items are met without serious or minor error. Two high-order points (HO1 and HO2) were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact: HO1 by reconciling reassuring neurologic exam/elevated BP with unresolved vascular risk, and HO2 by gently correcting the family’s conflation of all medicines as ‘通血管药’ and distinguishing anticoagulant from antiplatelet in plain language. No important non-chain defect remains. The closure is safe, executable, and traceable as valid_closure with teach-back evidence. The rubric therefore requires Strong (grade 4) because all RCs are met and exactly two authored high-order points were completed, meeting the Strong boundary but not the two-or-more fully distinct HO threshold for Perfect.",
